                      "title": "",
                      "passage": "Trees are one of the most important parts of our environment. They provide us with oxygen, which is necessary for humans and animals to live. Trees also give us fruits, wood, medicine, and shade. Their roots hold the soil together and help prevent soil erosion. Trees provide homes for many birds, insects, and animals.\n\nHowever, many trees are being cut down to build houses, roads, and factories. This can cause problems such as air pollution, loss of wildlife, and changes in the climate. Therefore, it is important for everyone to protect existing trees and plant new ones. Even a small effort, such as planting a tree in our neighbourhood, can make a difference.",
